The commit above is the head of meta pull request #107, "Fixture v6: what
separates scopes, and top-level keys ignoring case". That pull request is
merged with a merge commit, not squashed, so this commit lands on meta's main
unchanged; had it been squashed, the commit above would be replaced with the
squash commit, and the blob, bytes and sha256 would not change. Version 6 adds ten
calling-service cases and one gateway case and changes none. Only space, tab,
CR and LF separate scopes; VT, FF, a no-break space, an em space and every
other Unicode space are part of the scope token (2.0.0 split on `/\s+/` and
granted a scope the Go and Java clients refused). Two top-level keys equal
ignoring case are a duplicate, and a contract key spelled any other way is
malformed even once: 503 `centerUnavailable` on a calling service, the
`background` lane at the gateway (2.0.0 compared keys exactly). The fixture
pins ASCII case variants; this package lowers keys with `toLowerCase()`, as
the Java client does, and still refuses an exact repeat in any object at any
depth (src/strictJson.ts). 2.0.1 is the first release that passes version 6.

The sha256 is over the LF bytes of the blob as git stores it, which is what
`git show <commit>:fixtures/introspection.json` prints. test/conformance.test.ts
recomputes it on every run and fails if the vendored copy and this record ever
disagree, so a hand-edit of the copy is a red test rather than silent drift.

To re-vendor after meta changes the fixture:

  git -C ../meta show HEAD:fixtures/introspection.json > test/fixtures/introspection.json
  node -e "const c=require('crypto'),f=require('fs');const b=f.readFileSync('test/fixtures/introspection.json');console.log(b.length,c.createHash('sha256').update(b).digest('hex'))"

then update the commit, date, version, bytes and sha256 above. Change meta
first; a copy that leads the original is drift pointing the other way.

The conformance suite also asserts the sorted list of case names, so a case
added upstream fails here until it is implemented rather than being skipped.
